A1. What watered stock is preferred by colored investors? ~ MELON
A5. What does a second-hand car often refuse to do? ~ ACT
A8. What will an ex-service man get when he dies? ~ BONUS
A13. What is a baker's loafing place? ~ OVEN
A14. What is a yellow man's cue? ~ PLAIT
A16. What preparation of food contains everything from soup to nuts? ~ HASH
A17. What would a blind man like to do at a revue? ~ SEE
A18. What people end their days in the poorhouse? ~ PAUPERS
A20. What insect has a sweet disposition but a nose like a dentist's drill? ~ BEE
A21. What did the Mexican fruit vendor say when he had no bananas? ~ SI
A22. What is the safest point between Chicago and Shanghai? ~ MID
A23. What Southern State recently joined the wet column? (init.) ~ LA
A25. What is a specimen? ~ SAMPLE
A28. What material is used in the tailoring of bags? ~ BURLAP
A31. What is transferred from post to post? ~ MAIL
A32. What man in history was afflicted with boils and halitosis? ~ JOB
A34. What does a butcher buy at the stock market? ~ MEAT
A35. What coin is reserved fcr the collection plate? ~ CENT
A36. What appears when a swarm of moths chew the rag? ~ HOLES
A38. What do you do to feed the kitty? ~ ANTE
A40. What is a dust receptacle? ~ URN
A41. What is the theme of an old maid's dream? ~ MAN
A42. What did Col. Lindbergh do when he dined with the White House Sphinx? ~ ATE
A43. What metal is changed to gold in Henry Ford's mint? ~ TIN
A44. What did the convict do when he was choked by a necktie? ~ DIED
A46. What can an Italian do to reduce his taxes? ~ MARRY
A48. What would you call a pack of camels? ~ HERD
A49. What is a ten-footed, short-tailed crustacean? ~ CRAB
A51. What burden weighs heavily upon the shoulders of a bricklayer's assistant? ~ HOD
A52. What is the man who sits up to entertain his daughter's boy friends? ~ BORE
A53. What is Judge Junior's hat? ~ CASTOR
A54. What does the W. C. T. U. use as a tonic? ~ BRANDY
A56. Who is the big cheese in the En pire State? ~ AL
A57. What do people do at a bureau of information? ~ ASK
A59. What gives an old hen a pain in the neck? ~ AX
A60. What is the only secret a woman can keep? ~ AGE
A63. What is the fate that shapes our ends? ~ DESTINY
A66. What beverage is no longer popular in Boston? ~ TEA
A68. What is bootleg liquor everything else but? ~ PURE
A70. What did the Puritans carry to extremes? ~ PIETY
A71. What are the innocent victims of milk thieves? ~ COWS
A72. What did Napoleon meet at Waterloo? ~ ENEMY
A73. What word is part of the verb "to be"? ~ ARE
A74. What heavenly body often has a luminous train? ~ COMET

D1. Who was Grand Kleagle of the Jewish Klans? ~ MOSES
D2. Who promoted the first fruit exchange? ~ EVE
D3. What famous general was the idol of the South? ~ LEE
D4. What preposition means "above and touching"? ~ ON
D5. What astringent salt would make good lip-sticks for gossips? ~ ALUM
D6. What is the largest gas-house in the United States? ~ CAPITOL
D7. How is an ornamental knot made in a necktie? ~ TIED
D9. What exclamation denotes surprise? ~ OH
D10. How do the Mounted Police get their men? ~ NAB
D11. What word means to employ? ~ USE
D12. What ruminant animal often has its hair bobbed? ~ SHEEP
D14. What member of the family is noticed only on pay day? ~ PA
D15. What great statesman was the leader of the Rough Riders? (init.) ~ TR
D18. What is a drug store grenade? ~ PILL
D19. What is a low neighborhood? ~ SLUM
D21. What ean an expert tobacco chewer do with perfect control? ~ SPIT
D24. What are the great open spaces? ~ AREA
D26. What artificial desert is full of poison water holes? ~ AMERICA
D27. What does the man lack who appears in public in his B. V. D.'s? ~ MANNERS
D29. What started Paul Revere to running around? ~ LANTERN
D30. How does an artist's model feel when wearing a string of beads? ~ ATTIRED
D32. Who was the first person to make an under-sea voyage? ~ JONAH
D33. What should a man wear to hide his adam's apple? ~ BEARD
D35. What "chew" is used by most milk producers? ~ CUD
D36. What would you call a bad actor? ~ HAM
D37. What is a small imflammatory tumor on the edge of the eyelid? ~ STY
D39. What does a murderer often meet in the death house? ~ END
D45. What does an investigator spend most of his time trying to find? ~ DATA
D47. What domestic fowl resembles a hen and crows? ~ ROOSTER
D48. What is prohibition? ~ HOAX
D50. What will a woman be if she wears shorter skirts? ~ BOLD
D52. What harsh sound is made by an ass? ~ BRAY
D53. What are undertakers and reformers always hanging around? ~ CRAPE
D55. What is the cause of many uprisings? ~ YEAST
D57. Where is the best place to find nuts and washers? ~ ASIA
D58. What goes up in the air when covered with fly paper? ~ KITE
D61. What is a Chicago persuader? ~ GUN
D62. What word means "sooner than"? ~ ERE
D64. What is the abbreviation for Ephraim? ~ EP
D65. Where is Al Smith popular no end? (init.) ~ NY
D66. Who hangs around Kitty most of the evening? ~ TOM
D67. What do you call a female wool grower? ~ EWE
D69. What is a printer's measure? ~ EM
D71. What usually turns up over the week-end? (abbr.) ~ CO


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A35: What coin is reserved fcr the collection plate? → for
A56: Who is the big cheese in the En pire State? → Empire
D37: What is a small imflammatory tumor on the edge of the eyelid? → inflammatory

